{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# CrewAI: Role-Based Crews and Flows Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements stdlib versions of both shapes plus a three-agent crew."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Shape:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Agent`, `Task` dataclasses matching CrewAI's surface."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `SequentialCrew.kickoff(inputs)` runs tasks in declaration order, threading outputs as `context`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `HierarchicalCrew.kickoff(topic)` adds a manager Agent picking the next specialist each round, stops at \"done\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Flow` with `@start` and `@listen(topic)` decorators, a tiny event loop, and a trace."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `tool(name)` decorator mirroring CrewAI's `@tool` shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `Memory` with `short_term`, `long_term`, `entity` stores; mocked similarity uses numpy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Mock LLM responses are hardcoded strings keyed off role plus input prefix. No network. Deterministic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Concrete demo: researcher, writer, editor crew producing a brief on \"agent engineering 2026\". Researcher pulls (mocked) sources. Writer drafts. Editor tightens. Same crew runs through a Flow to show the deterministic shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Trace covers: sequential crew threading outputs through `context`, hierarchical crew with manager picks (researcher, writer, editor, then \"done\"), flow running the same three steps with explicit topics (`researched`, `drafted`, `edited`), tool calls routed through `@tool`, and long-term memory surviving across two kickoffs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The Crew trace is fluid; the manager could in principle re-order. The Flow trace is fixed. That choice is the lesson."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Convert the Sequential crew to a Flow. Count the touchpoints where variability drops. Note where readability dropped.\n2. Add entity memory to the crew: facts about a customer persist across kickoffs. Verify retrieval pulls the right entity.\n3. Implement a Hierarchical process where the manager refuses to route to the editor until the writer's output has at least three paragraphs. Trace the retry.\n4. Wire a `BaseTool` subclass for a (mocked) web search. Compare the trace shape vs the `@tool` decorator version.\n5. Add `output_pydantic=Brief` to the editor task, where `Brief` has `title`, `summary`, `sections`. Make the writer task output malformed JSON once; verify CrewAI's retry behavior in the trace.\n6. Read CrewAI's docs intro. Port the toy to the real `crewai` API. Which guarantees did the stdlib version skip?\n7. Wire AgentOps or Langfuse (Lesson 24) to a real run. Which traces did you miss in the stdlib version?"
      ]
    }
  ],
